      "id": 8966,
      "name": "Paul",
      "username": "Paul",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/paul/{size}/5862_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-11-05T17:30:23.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>A while back, I asked people about how frequently they check the GTG website for new news/content, and the general response was \"rarely to never\". This makes sense, since we've been really infrequent in our content updates and news posts.</p><p>Well, as of today, there are several changes that should help mitigate that problem, increasing both our ability to communicate with you awesome people (and a bunch of other people that want to follow along with GTG but not visit this wonderful forum). I made a recent News Post about it on the site (<a href=\"http://www.greaterthangames.com/news\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">www.greaterthangames.com/news</a>), but here is the summary:</p><p>1) Posts to the GTG News blog are now emailed out to our mailing list, and available as an RSS feed.</p><p>2) New News Posts and Official Tweets from <a href=\"https://twitter.com/GTGamesLLC\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">@GTGamesLLC</a> both now appear on the main site.</p><p>3) There is a new Blog, written principally about me, called the <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/journals/gtg-business-blog\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">GTG Business Blog</a>. It will typically cover general board game industry stuff, and will update every Tuesday and Thursday.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:37.846Z",
